      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-09T13:28:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we use same file for all the test failure instead of generating multiple file names? In this way, we can more easily to integrate with automatically method to fetch the file and attach to the bug later.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 65,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 65,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "1537aff2b27b396b5ea07f1db280125aa56c22cd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fd6b7e00_7e877762",
        "filename": "staticlibs/testutils/devicetests/com/android/testutils/ConnectivityDiagnosticsCollector.kt",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 65,
      "author": {
        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-10T00:27:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The test failure bugs should be per-method, or for a set of methods with similar failures, so I think one filename per test method is just what we need for that purpose.\nAnother use-case is to automatically aggregate data on what state the device is in when a method flakes (for example, \"90% of the time this method flakes, mobile data is disconnected\"), so having one file per method run would be more convenient for that too.\nIf we add several runs that happened at different times (possibly on different devices) to the same file I think that would be confusing, and having different method failures in the same file would require scrolling to find the section that matches the failure, which sounds inconvenient. But anyway, for the purposes of attaching a file to a test failure bug, since the bugs are per-method I think this already follows the same model.",
      "parentUuid": "4a8a0352_e58f4ad5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 65,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 65,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "1537aff2b27b396b5ea07f1db280125aa56c22cd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
